WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.874
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book three.

2
00:00:05.174 --> 00:00:08.653
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.953 --> 00:00:15.507
Unit two: Holidays & Celebrations. In this unit, you will talk about festivals and your holiday plans.

4
00:00:16.517 --> 00:00:17.297
Holiday.

5
00:00:17.997 --> 00:00:21.309
Holiday means a day or time when you do not work or go to school.

6
00:00:21.609 --> 00:00:23.631
Khmer New Year is my favorite holiday.

7
00:00:24.331 --> 00:00:27.077
Your turn. Say: Holiday.

8
00:00:29.777 --> 00:00:30.592
Holiday.

9
00:00:31.583 --> 00:00:32.468
Festival.

10
00:00:33.168 --> 00:00:37.130
Festival means a special time when people celebrate together.

11
00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:39.580
The Water Festival has boat races.

12
00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:42.735
Your turn. Say: Festival.

13
00:00:45.435 --> 00:00:46.390
Festival.

14
00:00:47.383 --> 00:00:48.199
Custom.

15
00:00:48.899 --> 00:00:51.781
Custom means something people in a place usually do.

16
00:00:52.081 --> 00:00:54.417
Pouring water on hands is a New Year custom.

17
00:00:55.117 --> 00:00:57.560
Your turn. Say: Custom.

18
00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.006
Custom.

19
00:01:02.017 --> 00:01:02.820
Gather.

20
00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:05.938
Gather means to come together in one place.

21
00:01:06.238 --> 00:01:08.516
My family gathers at Grandma's house.

22
00:01:09.216 --> 00:01:11.358
Your turn. Say: Gather.

23
00:01:14.058 --> 00:01:14.838
Gather.

24
00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:16.793
Decorate.

25
00:01:17.493 --> 00:01:19.841
Decorate means to make a place look beautiful.

26
00:01:20.141 --> 00:01:22.117
We decorate the house with flowers.

27
00:01:22.817 --> 00:01:25.493
Your turn. Say: Decorate.

28
00:01:28.193 --> 00:01:29.136
Decorate.

29
00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:30.768
Feast.

30
00:01:31.468 --> 00:01:33.270
Feast means a big special meal.

31
00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:35.523
We have a feast on the first day.

32
00:01:36.223 --> 00:01:38.283
Your turn. Say: Feast.

33
00:01:40.983 --> 00:01:41.729
Feast.

34
00:01:42.717 --> 00:01:43.636
Lantern.

35
00:01:44.336 --> 00:01:47.602
Lantern means a light inside a cover of paper or glass.

36
00:01:47.902 --> 00:01:49.808
Children carry lanterns at night.

37
00:01:50.508 --> 00:01:52.580
Your turn. Say: Lantern.

38
00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:56.165
Lantern.

39
00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:57.954
Firework.

40
00:01:58.654 --> 00:02:02.325
Firework means something that explodes with bright colors in the sky.

41
00:02:02.625 --> 00:02:04.706
We watched fireworks by the river.

42
00:02:05.406 --> 00:02:07.513
Your turn. Say: Firework.

43
00:02:10.213 --> 00:02:11.098
Firework.

44
00:02:12.083 --> 00:02:12.887
Parade.

45
00:02:13.587 --> 00:02:16.666
Parade means people walking or dancing through the streets.

46
00:02:16.966 --> 00:02:18.919
There is a big parade in the city.

47
00:02:19.619 --> 00:02:21.784
Your turn. Say: Parade.

48
00:02:24.484 --> 00:02:25.369
Parade.

49
00:02:26.383 --> 00:02:27.175
Reunion.

50
00:02:27.875 --> 00:02:31.733
Reunion means a meeting of people who have not seen each other for a long time.

51
00:02:32.033 --> 00:02:33.986
Pchum Ben is a family reunion.

52
00:02:34.686 --> 00:02:37.175
Your turn. Say: Reunion.

53
00:02:39.875 --> 00:02:40.679
Reunion.

54
00:02:41.683 --> 00:02:42.719
Ancestor.

55
00:02:43.419 --> 00:02:46.417
Ancestor means a family member who lived long ago.

56
00:02:46.717 --> 00:02:48.972
We remember our ancestors at Pchum Ben.

57
00:02:49.672 --> 00:02:52.034
Your turn. Say: Ancestor.

58
00:02:54.734 --> 00:02:55.851
Ancestor.

59
00:02:56.850 --> 00:02:57.596
Ritual.

60
00:02:58.296 --> 00:03:02.037
Ritual means a special act that people do in the same way each time.

61
00:03:02.337 --> 00:03:04.116
Monks lead a blessing ritual.

62
00:03:04.816 --> 00:03:07.816
Your turn. Say: Ritual.

63
00:03:10.516 --> 00:03:11.413
Ritual.

64
00:03:12.417 --> 00:03:14.532
Now let's listen to a conversation.

65
00:03:14.832 --> 00:03:17.807
Sreypich, what are you doing for Khmer New Year?

66
00:03:19.117 --> 00:03:21.523
I'm visiting my grandparents in Takeo.

67
00:03:22.817 --> 00:03:25.318
That sounds great! What are you doing there?

68
00:03:26.617 --> 00:03:29.185
We're decorating the house and having a big feast.

69
00:03:30.483 --> 00:03:32.181
Are you going to the pagoda?

70
00:03:33.483 --> 00:03:36.818
Yes, we're going on the first morning to give food to the monks.

71
00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:41.451
Grammar focus: Present continuous for plans.

72
00:03:41.751 --> 00:03:43.890
I'm visiting my grandparents next week.

73
00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:47.328
Use the present continuous for plans you have already made.

74
00:03:48.317 --> 00:03:51.050
Now read and listen. Our New Year Plans.

75
00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:53.385
Khmer New Year is coming in April.

76
00:03:54.683 --> 00:03:57.914
This year, my family is gathering at my grandparents' house.

77
00:03:59.217 --> 00:04:01.866
We're decorating the house with flowers and lanterns.

78
00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:06.520
On the first day, we're giving food to the monks at the pagoda.

79
00:04:07.817 --> 00:04:10.420
In the evening, we're having a big feast together.

80
00:04:11.717 --> 00:04:14.148
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

81
00:04:14.448 --> 00:04:16.727
We blank visiting Grandma next Sunday.

82
00:04:17.027 --> 00:04:19.391
A, are. B, is. C, am.

83
00:04:23.383 --> 00:04:25.244
The answer is A: are.

84
00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:28.750
A big special meal is a blank.

85
00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:32.448
A, feast. B, parade. C, ritual.

86
00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:38.345
The answer is A: feast.

87
00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:43.498
Family members who lived long ago are our blank.

88
00:04:43.798 --> 00:04:47.777
A, ancestors. B, neighbors. C, customs.

89
00:04:51.783 --> 00:04:53.980
The answer is A: ancestors.

90
00:04:55.483 --> 00:04:58.914
Now it's your turn to speak. What are you doing for the next holiday?

91
00:05:04.214 --> 00:05:09.559
I'm visiting my grandparents for Khmer New Year. We're decorating the house and having a feast together.

92
00:05:09.859 --> 00:05:11.545
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

93
00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:17.373
Great work today! You learned twelve new words and present continuous for plans.

94
00:05:17.673 --> 00:05:21.731
Today's value is togetherness. Spend happy time with your family.

95
00:05:22.031 --> 00:05:24.439
See you in Unit three. Goodbye!

96
00:05:24.739 --> 00:05:27.508
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

